    {
      "step": 2,
      "title": "Use the same truncated polynomial space",
      "text": "The monomials U_j=X^j and transformed Chebyshev polynomials Q_j=T_j composed with z each have degree j. Over the real field their leading coefficients are units. The canonical polynomial-sequence theorem shows that their first q+1 elements span precisely the same polynomial space. This is the triangular change of polynomial coordinates; it requires no independence of sampled vectors.",
